Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Yes. Just to respond, the Secretary has already spoken to Sen. Bong Go earlier

asr-001837
01:19:53.020 --> 01:19:55.020
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: and assured him that...

asr-001838
01:19:55.540 --> 01:20:00.180
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: She will be sending a team to address this issue.

asr-001839
01:20:00.180 --> 01:20:05.140
Senator Juan Miguel "Migz" F. Zubiri: I actually also asked the Electric Cooperative to write a formal letter.

asr-001840
01:20:05.140 --> 01:20:06.140
Senator Juan Miguel "Migz" F. Zubiri: So they did.

asr-001841
01:20:06.140 --> 01:20:08.980
Senator Juan Miguel "Migz" F. Zubiri: And then I submitted it to Sen. Bong Go.

asr-001842
01:20:08.980 --> 01:20:11.700
Senator Juan Miguel "Migz" F. Zubiri: But I don't think he was satisfied with the answer.

asr-001843
01:20:11.700 --> 01:20:15.760
Senator Juan Miguel "Migz" F. Zubiri: Because he said, well of course in the letter there was an outage from the NGCP at the same time.

asr-001844
01:20:15.760 --> 01:20:19.920
Senator Juan Miguel "Migz" F. Zubiri: There's also problems with yung punong kahoy, di ba?

asr-001845
01:20:19.920 --> 01:20:25.300
Senator Juan Miguel "Migz" F. Zubiri: Trees, yung tumatama sa poste, sa mga linya.

asr-001846
01:20:25.540 --> 01:20:27.220
Senator Juan Miguel "Migz" F. Zubiri: And they're clearing it out now.

asr-001847
01:20:27.340 --> 01:20:34.600
Senator Juan Miguel "Migz" F. Zubiri: But I guess maybe a more comprehensive answer would suffice and satisfy our distinguished colleague.

asr-001848
01:20:34.860 --> 01:20:35.460
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: Salamat po.

asr-001849
01:20:35.540 --> 01:20:40.280
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: Hindi lang naman po siguro ito sa Mindanao, sa Bukidnon and Dava Oriental itong problema nito.

asr-001850
01:20:40.380 --> 01:20:41.660
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: Sa buong Pilipinas po ito.

asr-001851
01:20:41.700 --> 01:20:44.400
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: And I'm sure alam niyo po yung mga reklamong yan.

asr-001852
01:20:44.500 --> 01:20:45.740
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: Sana matugunan po ito.

asr-001853
01:20:45.860 --> 01:20:50.760
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: Sana magkaroon na tayo ng brownout free dito sa ating bansa.

asr-001854
01:20:51.140 --> 01:20:52.000
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: Maraming salamat po.

asr-001855
01:20:52.300 --> 01:20:55.300
Senator Juan Miguel "Migz" F. Zubiri: Thank you, Sen. Bong Go for the short.

asr-001856
01:20:55.540 --> 01:20:56.460
Senator Juan Miguel "Migz" F. Zubiri: Intervention.

asr-001857
01:20:56.840 --> 01:21:02.600
Senator Juan Miguel "Migz" F. Zubiri: Mr. President, we'd now like to recognize the distinguished colleague, Sen. Rizal Tiveros, to propound some questions.

asr-001858
01:21:02.780 --> 01:21:04.420
Senate President Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Recognize Sen. Rizal Tiveros.

asr-001859
01:21:14.480 --> 01:21:17.980
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Salamat po, Mr. President. At magandang umaga po sa good sponsor.

asr-001860
01:21:19.280 --> 01:21:20.220
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Good morning.

asr-001861
01:21:20.620 --> 01:21:25.180
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Originally po, meron akong halos isang dosenang paksa.

asr-001862
01:21:25.180 --> 01:21:34.160
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Pero in the interest of time, kakalahatiin ko na lang sa lima, tatlo para sa DOE at dalawa para sa ERC.

asr-001863
01:21:34.740 --> 01:21:43.540
Senator Risa Hontiveros: And then, isasabit ko na lang, Mr. President, sa good sponsor yung ibang mga tanong ko para masagot ng department bago tayo dumako sa period of amendments.

asr-001864
01:21:45.620 --> 01:21:47.540
Senator Risa Hontiveros: So, una na po.

asr-001865
01:21:48.980 --> 01:21:54.600
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Mahigit isandaang gasolinahan na ang nahuli ng DOE.

asr-001866
01:21:55.180 --> 01:21:58.300
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Hindi sumusunod sa itinakdang rollback.

asr-001867
01:21:59.180 --> 01:22:01.200
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Yan ang nirereklamo ng mga motorista.

asr-001868
01:22:01.940 --> 01:22:04.240
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Pag price increase, ang pilis taasan.

asr-001869
01:22:04.940 --> 01:22:07.400
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Pero pag price decrease, ang bagal.

asr-001870
01:22:08.020 --> 01:22:14.160
Senator Risa Hontiveros: So, in effect, napipwersang magbayad ng overpriced rates kada litro ang consumers.

asr-001871
01:22:14.980 --> 01:22:19.620
Senator Risa Hontiveros: At kailangang mabawi rin ng mga motorista ang sobrang siningil sa kanila.

asr-001872
01:22:20.220 --> 01:22:25.160
Senator Risa Hontiveros: So, may paraan po ba ang DOE para tulungan ang consumers, Mr. President?

asr-001873
01:22:25.180 --> 01:22:30.860
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Kasi dapat mabawi nilang sobrang binayad nila.

asr-001875
01:22:51.980 --> 01:22:52.300
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Um,

asr-001876
01:22:53.180 --> 01:22:54.820
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: the result,

asr-001877
01:22:55.180 --> 01:23:16.740
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: The response, Your Honor, of DOE is that they issue show-cause orders, and then if there is a finding and there's a violation, then they can mete out the penalty. As to some kind of refund or compensation, they're still studying how to go about that.

asr-001878
01:23:16.740 --> 01:23:25.160
Senator Risa Hontiveros: All right. Salamat, good sponsor. May kailangan ba ang department sa budget natin para maipatupad ang mga ito?

asr-001879
01:23:30.140 --> 01:23:33.420
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: No, no. They just have to study how to go about it.

asr-001880
01:23:33.420 --> 01:23:46.500
Senator Risa Hontiveros: All right. And ngayon din mismo, may big time na rollback sa presyo ng petrolyo. Paano titiyakin ang department na tama yung presyo sa gas stations nationwide?

asr-001881
01:23:46.740 --> 01:23:51.060
Senator Risa Hontiveros: At ano ang magiging parusa sa mga lumabag at nag-overcharge?

asr-001882
01:23:52.640 --> 01:24:09.880
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: So, according to DOE, under RA 8479 and E0110, DOE is undertaking implementation of the mandated weekly price adjustment and monthly price adjustments,

asr-001883
01:24:09.880 --> 01:24:16.720
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: implementation of fuel subsidy discount programs. This is 12 pesos per liter on diesel of PUV.

asr-001884
01:24:16.740 --> 01:24:29.800
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: For a total of 1,000 pesos, 1,800 per week. Discount promos of the private oil companies and nationwide inspection to enforce the proper implementation of the DOE weekly mandated price adjustments.

asr-001885
01:24:31.200 --> 01:24:36.660
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Salamat po. May parusa ba kapag mayroon silang ma-identify na hindi sumunod sa rollback?

asr-001886
01:24:38.780 --> 01:24:42.960
Senator Risa Hontiveros: And again, sapat ba ang budget ng department para pagbantayan ito?

asr-001887
01:24:43.520 --> 01:24:43.960
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Okay.

asr-001888
01:24:44.560 --> 01:24:46.520
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: So, of course, they go through the process.

asr-001889
01:24:46.740 --> 01:24:55.780
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Your Honor, they have a show-cause order, and then when there's a finding, they can impose a penalty and in the worst case scenario, they can cancel the permit.

asr-001890
01:24:58.440 --> 01:24:59.080
Senator Risa Hontiveros: All right.

asr-001891
01:24:59.540 --> 01:25:05.600
Senator Risa Hontiveros: And tulad nung unang tanong, hindi na nila kailangan ng dagdag pang budget para gawin ang mga steps na ito?

asr-001892
01:25:05.600 --> 01:25:07.680
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Hindi na po. It's part of their mandate.

asr-001893
01:25:07.760 --> 01:25:08.480
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: All right.

asr-001894
01:25:09.980 --> 01:25:13.900
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: And they have the support of the DILG and then the LGUs.

asr-001895
01:25:14.280 --> 01:25:14.720
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Okay.

asr-001896
01:25:15.800 --> 01:25:16.460
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: And PNP.

asr-001897
01:25:16.740 --> 01:25:17.740
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Okay.

asr-001898
01:25:18.240 --> 01:25:18.880
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Good po.

asr-001899
01:25:19.380 --> 01:25:19.780
Senator Risa Hontiveros: All right.

asr-001900
01:25:20.960 --> 01:25:21.640
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Sunod po.

asr-001901
01:25:22.060 --> 01:25:26.920
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Wala pa mga ELNINIO noon, nararanasan natin ang brownout.

asr-001902
01:25:27.060 --> 01:25:31.060
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Yellow alerts at red alerts lalo na sa Visayas at Mindanao.

asr-001903
01:25:31.820 --> 01:25:44.540
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Dapat po may nakalaan na sa 2027 budget ng DOE para masigurong tuloy-tuloy ang operasyon ng lalo na ating mga ospital at ating mga eskwelahan

asr-001904
01:25:44.540 --> 01:25:46.260
Senator Risa Hontiveros: sakaling lumala ang kakulangan.

asr-001905
01:25:46.740 --> 01:25:49.160
Senator Risa Hontiveros: ng supply ng kuryente.

asr-001906
01:25:49.880 --> 01:25:55.860
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Magkano po ang inilaan natin para dito at ano yung mga kaakibat na contingency plans ng department?

asr-001907
01:25:56.100 --> 01:25:56.760
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Mr. President?

asr-001908
01:26:16.740 --> 01:26:35.180
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: So, according to the Secretary, Your Honor, hospitals and schools are mandated to have their backup gensets available and they continue to monitor this.

asr-001909
01:26:35.180 --> 01:26:44.240
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: And then there is also a NDRR MC Resolution No. 2 Series of 2026 that provides for the standards.

asr-001910
01:26:44.860 --> 01:26:46.660
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: We can give Her Honor a copy.

asr-001911
01:26:47.600 --> 01:26:48.380
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Salamat po.

asr-001912
01:26:49.020 --> 01:26:52.340
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Ano yung item na nakalaan na sa budget para sa mga ito?

asr-001916
01:26:58.300 --> 01:27:02.940
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Okay. So, for example, for the hospitals and schools, it's in their specific budgets.

asr-001917
01:27:03.160 --> 01:27:04.360
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Ah, okay. Individually.

asr-001918
01:27:05.240 --> 01:27:15.560
Senator Risa Hontiveros: At the same time, good sponsor, Mr. President, sa ganyang mga pagkakataon, mas lalong dapat isama sa pinupondohan natin ang solar at saka battery storage.

asr-001919
01:27:16.740 --> 01:27:20.500
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Sa mga public hospitals, public schools, actually, pati sa mga SUCs.

asr-001920
01:27:20.860 --> 01:27:24.780
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Tulad ng sinimula na ngayon sa UP Solarization Project.

asr-001921
01:27:25.300 --> 01:27:28.220
Senator Risa Hontiveros: At especially kung madalas mag-brown out.

asr-001922
01:27:28.760 --> 01:27:35.680
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Nakwenta na rin ba natin kung magkanong kailangan para mais ako tuparan ito sa buong bansa?

asr-001923
01:27:38.960 --> 01:27:46.360
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: So, actually, yung binanggit ko na NDRR MC Resolution No. 2, 2026,

asr-001924
01:27:46.740 --> 01:27:52.880
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: kasama dyan, solar PV with battery storage, ang preferred, ano talaga, source, no?

asr-001925
01:27:53.280 --> 01:28:08.780
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: And then, yung funding source ng mga LGU would be coming from the local DRRM fund, national DRRM fund, ER-194 fund, climate finance, and other eligible funding sources.

asr-001926
01:28:09.040 --> 01:28:13.440
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Alright. So, hindi na po kailangan ng may dagdag pang items sa DOE budget separately.

asr-001927
01:28:13.840 --> 01:28:14.720
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Alright. Salamat po.

asr-001928
01:28:14.920 --> 01:28:16.720
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Bago yung huling paksakot...

asr-001929
01:28:16.740 --> 01:28:35.060
Senator Risa Hontiveros: So, sa last on this particular topic, dun sa budget na meron tayo sa 2027, ilan ang kaya nating maseribisyohan in terms of the schools and hospitals?

asr-001932
01:28:46.740 --> 01:28:57.500
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: So, actually, as mentioned earlier, this is already in the budgets of the respective institutions.

asr-001933
01:28:57.780 --> 01:29:04.500
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: So, kung sa school, nasa school, hospital, nasa hospital. So, nandiyan na ho yun, they're supposed to budget for that already.

asr-001934
01:29:04.500 --> 01:29:14.600
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Alright. Then, bago nga yung huling paksakot sa DOE, one step back dun sa unang paksa, tungkol sa paanong bababawi ng consumer yung sobrang binayad nila,

asr-001935
01:29:14.600 --> 01:29:26.320
Senator Risa Hontiveros: meron din bang pinag-aaralan ng DOE na paraan ng, kung hindi diretsyong refund, pag natabi nung customer yung resibo nila,

asr-001936
01:29:26.760 --> 01:29:35.900
Senator Risa Hontiveros: pagbalik dun sa gasolinahan kung saan sobra palang binayad nila noon, may paraan ba na ma-offset yung susunod na babayaran nila?

asr-001937
01:29:36.760 --> 01:29:40.500
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Masama yun. Masama yun, your honor, dun sa pinag-aaralan nila.

asr-001938
01:29:40.500 --> 01:29:42.200
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Okay. Alright. Salamat.

asr-001939
01:29:42.480 --> 01:29:43.500
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Huling paksa ako sa DOE.

asr-001940
01:29:44.600 --> 01:29:45.760
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Sir President, good sponsor.

asr-001941
01:29:46.460 --> 01:29:56.020
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Noong Setiembre, sinabi ng DOE na target nila ang zero brownout sa Visayas at sa Mindanao ngayong papasok na Disyembre.

asr-001942
01:29:56.840 --> 01:29:59.200
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Magagaransya ba ng department?

asr-001943
01:30:00.000 --> 01:30:06.160
Senator Risa Hontiveros: na walang brownout at maliwanag ang Pasko ng mga pamilyang Pilipino.

asr-001944
01:30:08.320 --> 01:30:12.580
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Makakapagsindi ba ng parol ang bawat pamilyang Pilipino ngayong Pasko?

asr-001945
01:30:30.000 --> 01:30:39.220
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: So, her honor is correct that that is the objective.

asr-001946
01:30:39.500 --> 01:30:40.260
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: That is the objective.

asr-001947
01:30:40.880 --> 01:30:49.740
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: So, what they can do, what is within their power is to make sure that everything that is required to happen is in place.

asr-001948
01:30:49.840 --> 01:30:50.960
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: So, they're doing all that.

asr-001949
01:30:51.100 --> 01:30:57.980
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: They're doing all that, making sure that the power plants are functioning up to par, etc., etc.

asr-001950
01:30:57.980 --> 01:30:59.980
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: So, it goes without saying.

asr-001951
01:31:00.000 --> 01:31:09.100
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: So, it goes without saying that if in place lahat ito, then the chances of being successful in what we want to achieve, which is zero brownout, will happen.

asr-001952
01:31:12.100 --> 01:31:20.860
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Natansya ba nila? Ano yung percentage na chance na ma-achieve nga yung objective na ito by next month sa Visayas at Mindanao?

asr-001956
01:31:39.220 --> 01:31:43.860
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Let's try to understand the reason for the brownouts.

asr-001957
01:31:44.420 --> 01:31:47.420
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Mangyayari yan kung mag-fail yung power plants.

asr-001958
01:31:47.880 --> 01:31:49.700
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Kaya, ang gagawin nila, address nila yun.

asr-001959
01:31:51.000 --> 01:31:53.280
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Ensure that these power plants can perform.

asr-001960
01:31:53.860 --> 01:31:55.820
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: So, that is additional reserves.

asr-001961
01:31:55.820 --> 01:31:57.620
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: So, reserves is already the backup, di ba?

asr-001962
01:31:57.700 --> 01:31:58.600
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: I assume mo na na.

asr-001963
01:31:59.220 --> 01:32:02.080
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: I think that's part of the, what's the term there?

asr-001964
01:32:02.200 --> 01:32:07.440
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Yung proper maintenance and to assure steady supply is may reserve ka.

asr-001965
01:32:07.680 --> 01:32:10.480
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: It's one thing to say na wala yan, tas wala kang reserve.

asr-001966
01:32:10.640 --> 01:32:12.180
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: I mean, it won't happen, wala kang reserve.

asr-001967
01:32:12.280 --> 01:32:20.200
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: So, that's already being responsible by ensuring that there's additional reserves and incoming generating capacity, intergrid transfers.

asr-001968
01:32:20.900 --> 01:32:25.220
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: This is all intended to prevent the supply-related interruptions.

asr-001969
01:32:26.220 --> 01:32:27.740
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: So, they're doing all that.

asr-001970
01:32:29.220 --> 01:32:35.760
Senator Risa Hontiveros: So, I believe, Mr. President, what the good sponsor is saying, that the department is doing all that.

asr-001971
01:32:36.140 --> 01:32:38.540
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Lalo na dahil yung department ang nag-set ng target.

asr-001972
01:32:38.760 --> 01:32:43.500
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Wala pong nag-impose sa kanila na wala ng brownouts sa Visayas at Mindanao by December.

asr-001973
01:32:44.120 --> 01:32:48.980
Senator Risa Hontiveros: So, can they promise na makakasindi ng parolang bawat pamilyang Pilipino?

asr-001974
01:32:49.620 --> 01:32:57.180
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Or may percentage ba that they think they will be achieving the self-imposed target by next month?

asr-001975
01:32:57.180 --> 01:32:59.080
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: So, I think I've answered that.

asr-001976
01:32:59.220 --> 01:33:02.840
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Your Honor, to the best of DOE's ability to respond.

asr-001977
01:33:03.320 --> 01:33:06.060
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: So, they can't give us an estimate?

asr-001978
01:33:06.560 --> 01:33:10.180
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Kasi, Your Honor, what they can do nga, as I said, and as I will repeat,

asr-001979
01:33:10.620 --> 01:33:18.540
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: is they are doing everything to ensure that itong power plants are functioning and then may reserve.

asr-001980
01:33:19.220 --> 01:33:20.300
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: That's what they can do.

asr-001981
01:33:20.580 --> 01:33:25.520
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: So, if they do that, then the chances of having brownouts is very minimal.

asr-001982
01:33:25.940 --> 01:33:27.940
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: They would have given me a percentage.

asr-001983
01:33:29.220 --> 01:33:32.680
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: I've heard her Honor's question, but I guess they're not able to really give that.

asr-001984
01:33:32.760 --> 01:33:35.120
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: But they want to give that assurance as best as they can.

asr-001985
01:33:37.400 --> 01:33:42.120
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Well, I guess I'll have to accept that answer from the department.

asr-001986
01:33:42.940 --> 01:33:46.160
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Disappointing lang kasi ang ganda sana nung target na naset.

asr-001987
01:33:46.360 --> 01:33:52.880
Senator Risa Hontiveros: And I'm sure umasay yung mga kababayan natin sa Visayas at Mindanao by next month.

asr-001988
01:33:52.880 --> 01:33:58.900
Senator Risa Hontiveros: And for the record, Mr. President, good sponsor, tayo dito sa Senado, when we set targets,

asr-001989
01:33:59.220 --> 01:34:04.620
Senator Risa Hontiveros: and then we ask each other sa mga komite natin, halimbawa, ano na yung progress report,

asr-001990
01:34:04.880 --> 01:34:08.560
Senator Risa Hontiveros: more or less, we are able to put a number to our own target.

asr-001991
01:34:08.720 --> 01:34:11.440
Senator Risa Hontiveros: So, I was expecting more from the department.

asr-001992
01:34:11.680 --> 01:34:17.040
Senator Risa Hontiveros: And maybe by the time of the period of amendments, they can come up with a better answer for us

asr-001993
01:34:17.040 --> 01:34:22.440
Senator Risa Hontiveros: at sa mga kababayan natin, lalo na who are hoping for a brighter Christmas

asr-001994
01:34:22.440 --> 01:34:27.800
Senator Risa Hontiveros: than they have experienced in the past months or this whole year, actually.

asr-001995
01:34:28.100 --> 01:34:29.060
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Good sponsor.

asr-001997
01:34:29.220 --> 01:34:29.880
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Mr. President.

asr-001998
01:34:32.460 --> 01:34:40.820
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Magkano po yung inilaan natin sa 2027 budget para tuluyan na nga matugunan ang problema sa brownout sa Visayas at Mindanao?

asr-001999
01:34:59.220 --> 01:35:29.200
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: So, um, Your Honor, these are private-sector commitments, no? And so what DOE is doing is they're keeping abreast of what's happening, keeping track of the commitments, particularly on battery and barges, kasi diyan ho nanggagaling yung reserve. Kaya nga, like I said,

asr-002000
01:35:29.220 --> 01:35:34.800
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: There's a supply, but the backup there is to have the reserve.

asr-002001
01:35:34.900 --> 01:35:36.200
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: That's very, very important.

asr-002002
01:35:36.460 --> 01:35:43.120
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: So, they're not literally the ones in charge of those reserves, but they're on top of it,

asr-002003
01:35:43.660 --> 01:35:48.620
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: ensuring that ito nga, yung batteries and the barges are in place.

asr-002004
01:35:49.200 --> 01:35:52.540
Senator Risa Hontiveros: And magkano pong inilaan, Mr. President, para sa barges at sa batteries?

asr-002005
01:35:52.540 --> 01:35:54.800
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: It's a private endeavor, as I said, Your Honor.

asr-002006
01:35:55.080 --> 01:35:55.600
Senator Risa Hontiveros: It's private.

asr-002007
01:35:55.600 --> 01:35:58.920
Senator Risa Hontiveros: But is the DOE not able to disclose to us?

asr-002008
01:35:59.220 --> 01:36:00.420
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Here in Congress?

asr-002009
01:36:00.640 --> 01:36:01.820
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Those are separate contracts.

asr-002010
01:36:02.040 --> 01:36:04.200
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Would you like a list of those contracts?

asr-002011
01:36:04.220 --> 01:36:05.680
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Sure, Mr. President.

asr-002012
01:36:05.760 --> 01:36:06.940
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Again, we'll ask them to provide, Your Honor.

asr-002013
01:36:07.120 --> 01:36:07.580
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Okay, salamat.

asr-002014
01:36:08.480 --> 01:36:12.560
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Moving on to my couple of topics para sa ERC.

asr-002015
01:36:13.420 --> 01:36:18.580
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Ang pinakamahalagang tungkulin ng ERC ay pagpapababa sa presyo ng kuryente

asr-002016
01:36:18.580 --> 01:36:21.380
Senator Risa Hontiveros: at pagtatanggol sa kapakanan ng mga consumer.

asr-002017
01:36:21.380 --> 01:36:28.380
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Sa tulong ng budget na binigay sa commission,

asr-002018
01:36:28.380 --> 01:36:30.380
Senator Risa Hontiveros: para sa 2027,

asr-002019
01:36:31.220 --> 01:36:36.820
Senator Risa Hontiveros: magkano ang aasahan o target ng ahensya na pagbabasa singil sa consumer

asr-002020
01:36:36.820 --> 01:36:40.820
Senator Risa Hontiveros: ng mga distribution utilities next year, Mr. President?

asr-002021
01:36:48.060 --> 01:36:50.780
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Can I just ask the question to be repeated?

asr-002022
01:36:50.920 --> 01:36:53.720
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Because even if you pass me the answer, I want to hear the question myself.

asr-002023
01:36:53.720 --> 01:36:57.720
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Magkano ang aasahan o target ng ERC

asr-002024
01:36:57.720 --> 01:36:58.320
Senator Risa Hontiveros: na pagbaba sa

asr-002027
01:36:58.380 --> 01:37:02.240
Senator Risa Hontiveros: singil sa consumer ng mga distribution utilities next year.

asr-002028
01:37:02.400 --> 01:37:03.760
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Yes, Mr. President.

asr-002029
01:37:28.380 --> 01:37:47.000
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: So, to be clear, Your Honor, the mandate of ERC is to ensure that the investments in the generation and transmission are bare fruit.

asr-002030
01:37:47.000 --> 01:37:56.120
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Because if this is accomplished, then it will naturally happen that the prices will go down.

asr-002031
01:37:56.320 --> 01:37:58.180
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Paso supply and demand lang po yun, Your Honor.

asr-002032
01:37:58.180 --> 01:38:08.700
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Kung nandyan yung capacity to provide, then there will be enough supply and the prices will come down at a lower.

asr-002033
01:38:08.800 --> 01:38:11.440
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Pag kulang ang supply, edi nagmamahal.

asr-002034
01:38:11.560 --> 01:38:15.620
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: So, that is the mandate of ERC, to ensure that this is in place.

asr-002035
01:38:16.780 --> 01:38:26.580
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Unfortunately, Mr. President, good sponsor, yun na nga yung pangako sa ilalim ng EPIRA at doon na nga dinerive yung ganyang mandate ng ERC.

asr-002036
01:38:26.580 --> 01:38:39.380
Senator Risa Hontiveros: And although there have been numerous investments in the last quarter century at maraming private sector stakeholders ay kumita,

asr-002037
01:38:39.840 --> 01:38:47.040
Senator Risa Hontiveros: hindi pa natin na-achieve yung least cost price para sa mga consumers.

asr-002038
01:38:47.240 --> 01:38:51.620
Senator Risa Hontiveros: So, hindi purely nag-ooperate yung law of supply and demand dito.

asr-002039
01:38:51.620 --> 01:38:56.540
Senator Risa Hontiveros: So, given that hindi pa optimal.

asr-002040
01:38:56.580 --> 01:39:03.580
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Na situation, meron din bang tansya ang ERC kung by how much bababa ang singil,

asr-002041
01:39:04.420 --> 01:39:09.920
Senator Risa Hontiveros: pagsingil sa customers ng mga distribution utilities sa 2027.

asr-002042
01:39:26.580 --> 01:39:47.020
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: The first thing that they are doing to address this concern, which is yung mataas na presyo,

asr-002043
01:39:47.020 --> 01:39:51.900
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: at yung goal naman is very clear na bumaba sana ang presyo, is addressing the backlog.

asr-002044
01:39:52.040 --> 01:39:56.420
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: That I know, kasi in the years that I was chairman of the...

asr-002045
01:39:56.420 --> 01:40:01.800
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: of the Committee on Energy, that really has been an ongoing concern.

asr-002046
01:40:01.980 --> 01:40:03.480
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Like talagang grabe yung backlog.

asr-002047
01:40:03.760 --> 01:40:10.800
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: So, I remember when the last hearing I had, that's really something that was highlighted by ERC.

asr-002048
01:40:11.040 --> 01:40:13.400
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: And then second is yung rate reset.

asr-002049
01:40:14.120 --> 01:40:15.400
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Tinatrabaho talaga nila yun.

asr-002050
01:40:15.820 --> 01:40:20.240
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Now, as to her honor's specific question, magkano.

asr-002051
01:40:21.060 --> 01:40:24.660
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: It's difficult to answer because as I said, supply and demand.

asr-002052
01:40:24.660 --> 01:40:26.280
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: And a lot of things.

asr-002053
01:40:26.420 --> 01:40:30.040
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: But going to the price are beyond the control of ERC.

asr-002054
01:40:30.220 --> 01:40:34.440
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: And as her honor knows, the peso, like hindi naman...

asr-002055
01:40:34.440 --> 01:40:41.080
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: I don't think anyone had expected na ganito kasama yung exchange rate natin ngayon.

asr-002056
01:40:41.180 --> 01:40:41.880
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: And it's bad.

asr-002057
01:40:42.340 --> 01:40:43.600
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: I think no one can say that.

asr-002058
01:40:43.820 --> 01:40:51.320
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: And then yung price ng fuel natin talagang mataas.

asr-002059
01:40:51.320 --> 01:40:54.220
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: So, those factors are changing.

asr-002060
01:40:55.060 --> 01:40:55.320
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: So...

asr-002061
01:40:55.320 --> 01:40:59.340
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: So, if let's say all of these things are in place na na-address yung backlog,

asr-002062
01:40:59.620 --> 01:41:06.020
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: pero God forbid na sobrang tumangit yung ating peso rate,

asr-002063
01:41:06.640 --> 01:41:08.840
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: then yung pinapredict nila magbabago din.

asr-002064
01:41:09.200 --> 01:41:12.700
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: I think her honor can understand that kasi there's a lot of...

asr-002065
01:41:12.700 --> 01:41:15.260
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Parang commodities yan eh na nagbabago talaga yung price.

asr-002066
01:41:15.260 --> 01:41:25.260
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: But I think we are one in hoping that with at least the two major issues,

asr-002067
01:41:25.320 --> 01:41:29.540
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: efforts of ERC, which is addressing the backlog and the rate reset,

asr-002068
01:41:29.800 --> 01:41:31.680
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: it's going in the right direction.

asr-002069
01:41:31.820 --> 01:41:33.160
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Dun sa pababa yung presyo.

asr-002070
01:41:34.700 --> 01:41:38.000
Senator Risa Hontiveros: I'm beginning to see a pattern here, Mr. President.

asr-002071
01:41:38.140 --> 01:41:47.760
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Good sponsor sa sagot ng mga agencies natin na hindi makapagbigay ni ng target

asr-002072
01:41:47.760 --> 01:41:52.640
Senator Risa Hontiveros: or reasonable commitment.

asr-002073
01:41:53.440 --> 01:41:53.760
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Given...

asr-002074
01:41:54.480 --> 01:41:54.760
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Target...

asr-002075
01:41:55.320 --> 01:41:59.660
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Target na siya mismo nag-set in the case of DOE nung Setyembre

asr-002076
01:41:59.660 --> 01:42:06.000
Senator Risa Hontiveros: or mandate nila sa ilalim ng batas in the case of ERC.

asr-002077
01:42:06.500 --> 01:42:13.340
Senator Risa Hontiveros: We could talk a lot also about that rate reset, kung paano mas maayos na ginagawa yan ng ERC.

asr-002078
01:42:13.340 --> 01:42:17.300
Senator Risa Hontiveros: But ERC is not as powerless as they say they are.

asr-002079
01:42:17.840 --> 01:42:23.660
Senator Risa Hontiveros: May mga kapangyarihan din ng ERC kahit sa ilalim ng EPIRA

asr-002080
01:42:23.660 --> 01:42:25.200
Senator Risa Hontiveros: that they could afford to...

asr-002081
01:42:25.320 --> 01:42:33.060
Senator Risa Hontiveros: to exercise more assertively and proactively alang-alang sa mga consumers.

asr-002082
01:42:33.800 --> 01:42:35.960
Senator Risa Hontiveros: So, niwala ba silang target?

asr-002083
01:42:38.740 --> 01:42:40.020
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Kaiba ba ang singil?

asr-002084
01:42:40.520 --> 01:42:45.440
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Can they only tell us yung mga external factors na di umano,

asr-002085
01:42:45.580 --> 01:42:47.420
Senator Risa Hontiveros: nag-gumagapo sa kamay nila?

asr-002086
01:42:47.960 --> 01:42:49.980
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Given their powers under the EPIRA,

asr-002087
01:42:49.980 --> 01:42:54.400
Senator Risa Hontiveros: are they not even going to try to set a target for next year?

asr-002088
01:42:54.820 --> 01:42:55.180
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Mr. President...

asr-002089
01:42:55.320 --> 01:42:56.200
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Mr. President, good sponsor.

asr-002090
01:43:02.920 --> 01:43:06.660
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Maybe, Mr. President, ERC should also study or explore

asr-002091
01:43:06.660 --> 01:43:11.840
Senator Risa Hontiveros: capping, fuel, and forex cost pass-through to consumers.

asr-002092
01:43:17.540 --> 01:43:19.900
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Magagawa ba natin ito through regulations?

asr-002093
01:43:20.080 --> 01:43:24.060
Senator Risa Hontiveros: O kailangan pa ba intayin yung amendments sa EPIRA para gawin ito?

asr-002095
01:43:55.320 --> 01:44:09.240
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Your Honor, according to ERC, of the total electricity bill,

asr-002096
01:44:10.440 --> 01:44:15.420
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: what they can regulate is 25% of that.

asr-002097
01:44:15.420 --> 01:44:18.980
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: So 75% is beyond their control.

asr-002098
01:44:18.980 --> 01:44:27.200
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: So in the case of the generation charges,

asr-002099
01:44:28.180 --> 01:44:39.540
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: if her Honor is suggesting or asking that this be capped,

asr-002100
01:44:40.220 --> 01:44:43.840
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: then for ERC, it would be very difficult for them

asr-002101
01:44:43.840 --> 01:44:48.960
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: to attract investments on that.

asr-002102
01:44:48.980 --> 01:44:50.800
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: On that side, on the generation side,

asr-002103
01:44:50.940 --> 01:44:53.920
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: kasi mahirap na yung supplier,

asr-002104
01:44:54.060 --> 01:44:55.600
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: sasabihin mo hanggang ganito lang,

asr-002105
01:44:56.260 --> 01:44:59.980
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: pero yung kinukunan niyang...

asr-002106
01:45:00.000 --> 01:45:10.560
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: main ano niya is so much more expensive because of factors beyond their control like the war, the depreciation rate, that is not beyond their control.

asr-002107
01:45:10.700 --> 01:45:18.400
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: So kung itatali sila ng ERC, baka huwalang pumayag kasi nga kahit sila, it's beyond their control, Your Honor.

asr-002108
01:45:19.320 --> 01:45:24.120
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Well, nabanggit Mr. President ng Good Sponsor yung generation charges.

asr-002109
01:45:24.120 --> 01:45:40.680
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Isa yun sa mga tanong na isasubmit ko na lang sa Good Sponsor para sa ERC dahil kung yung system loss charge ay 5 to 10 percent sa bill na pinapason sa consumers,

asr-002110
01:45:40.820 --> 01:45:45.400
Senator Risa Hontiveros: yung generation charges ang pinakamalaki, constituting around 60 percent.

asr-002111
01:45:45.400 --> 01:45:53.480
Senator Risa Hontiveros: And naka-fold in pa doon yung cost of fuel na hindi pa fully dinidisclose ng lahat.

asr-002112
01:45:53.780 --> 01:45:54.100
Senator Risa Hontiveros: So,

asr-002113
01:45:54.120 --> 01:45:59.060
Senator Risa Hontiveros: ng mga generation companies.

asr-002114
01:45:59.980 --> 01:46:06.220
Senator Risa Hontiveros: At ang tanong kong isasubmit ko dyan sa Good Sponsor ay tungkol sa pag-review ng mga power supply agreements.

asr-002115
01:46:10.220 --> 01:46:21.360
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Huling paksa ko para sa ERC, and ito, pangatlong beses ko na pong itatanong sa ERC, yung pag-audit na mga fuel pass-through ng generation companies nga po.

asr-002116
01:46:21.360 --> 01:46:23.780
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Isa sa mga bagay na tinatanong din ang

asr-002117
01:46:23.780 --> 01:46:25.400
Senator Risa Hontiveros: ating Senate President.

asr-002118
01:46:26.120 --> 01:46:28.880
Senator Risa Hontiveros: May resulta na ba ang review ng ERC?

asr-002119
01:46:29.360 --> 01:46:35.220
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Kasi sabi po ng Commission dati na ayaw itong i-disclose ng mga generation companies.

asr-002120
01:46:40.640 --> 01:46:44.700
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: I can read to you, Your Honor, what was given to me.

asr-002121
01:46:45.160 --> 01:46:53.540
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Based on the audit procedure approved by the Commission, 10 DUs and generating companies pairs were identified.

asr-002123
01:46:53.640 --> 01:46:58.840
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: To be part of the first batch to be subjected to fuel audit, they were selected based on the

asr-002124
01:46:58.840 --> 01:47:10.040
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: A, size of consumer exposure, this is the DU's total energy sales, and B, magnitude of the fuel cost increase, the blended generation rate billed during the period.

asr-002125
01:47:10.520 --> 01:47:17.820
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: By assigning equal weight to these criteria, the prioritization methodology ensures that the audit captures the DU-GENCO pairs

asr-002126
01:47:17.820 --> 01:47:23.480
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: that not only exhibit significant fuel cost-related increases, but also have the,

asr-002128
01:47:23.620 --> 01:47:30.540
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: greatest potential impact on consumers, consistent with the objectives of the approved audit procedure.

asr-002129
01:47:31.660 --> 01:47:39.700
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: The audit team has completed evaluating the documents submitted by one DU-GENCO pair, which was included in the initial batch.

asr-002130
01:47:40.100 --> 01:47:45.180
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: An exit conference will be scheduled with the said pair before the audit report is finalized.

asr-002131
01:47:45.320 --> 01:47:50.360
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Evaluation of the other GENCO-DU pairs, their submission is ongoing.

asr-002132
01:47:50.360 --> 01:47:53.500
Senator Risa Hontiveros: So, may unang pair na.

asr-002133
01:47:53.620 --> 01:47:54.320
Senator Risa Hontiveros: So, may walo pa.

asr-002134
01:47:54.960 --> 01:47:56.340
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Apat na pairs pa ang pending.

asr-002135
01:47:56.700 --> 01:47:59.800
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Mga kailan daw nila matatapos good sponsor yung audit na ito?

asr-002136
01:47:59.920 --> 01:48:01.300
Senator Risa Hontiveros: At is nung first batch?

asr-002137
01:48:01.440 --> 01:48:01.860
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Ten pairs.

asr-002138
01:48:01.900 --> 01:48:02.340
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Ah, siyam.

asr-002139
01:48:02.580 --> 01:48:03.820
Senator Risa Hontiveros: So, siyam pa.

asr-002140
01:48:03.920 --> 01:48:04.280
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Ten pairs.

asr-002141
01:48:04.500 --> 01:48:05.280
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Ten pairs, yes.

asr-002142
01:48:05.660 --> 01:48:10.140
Senator Risa Hontiveros: So, may timetable po ba sila para makumpleto itong unang batch na review?

asr-002144
01:48:12.820 --> 01:48:14.520
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: By first quarter of next year, Your Honor.

asr-002145
01:48:14.940 --> 01:48:15.380
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Ah, alright.

asr-002146
01:48:15.660 --> 01:48:16.960
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Soon enough, good sponsor.

asr-002147
01:48:18.860 --> 01:48:23.460
Senator Risa Hontiveros: May kakailanganin pa ba sa budget ng ERC sa susunod na taon para,

asr-002148
01:48:23.460 --> 01:48:25.760
Senator Risa Hontiveros: para makumpleto ang fuel audit na ito?

asr-002149
01:48:26.660 --> 01:48:28.620
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: No, they can handle it, Your Honor.

asr-002150
01:48:29.660 --> 01:48:30.020
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Alright.

asr-002151
01:48:30.780 --> 01:48:35.200
Senator Risa Hontiveros: And kapag nakumpleto na nila ito, first quarter next year,

asr-002152
01:48:35.340 --> 01:48:39.560
Senator Risa Hontiveros: pwede po bang magkaroon ng kopya ang kongreso ng mga resultang ito?

asr-002153
01:48:39.880 --> 01:48:41.460
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Yes, ang sagot po nila is yes.

asr-002154
01:48:41.660 --> 01:48:42.960
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Salamat, good sponsor.

asr-002155
01:48:43.300 --> 01:48:46.300
Senator Risa Hontiveros: So, sa pagwawakas ko, Mr. President, good sponsor,

asr-002156
01:48:46.780 --> 01:48:51.460
Senator Risa Hontiveros: ulitin ko na lang yung sana naman pagdating ng period of amendments,

asr-002157
01:48:51.460 --> 01:48:53.460
Senator Risa Hontiveros: may maisagot na ang...

asr-002158
01:48:53.460 --> 01:48:54.940
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Department of Energy.

asr-002159
01:48:56.620 --> 01:49:02.780
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Kahit hindi 100%, basta some concrete and realistic commitment

asr-002160
01:49:02.780 --> 01:49:08.940
Senator Risa Hontiveros: na sa mga pamilya at households Pilipino,

asr-002161
01:49:09.080 --> 01:49:10.460
Senator Risa Hontiveros: lalo na sa Visayas at Mindanao,

asr-002162
01:49:11.560 --> 01:49:14.460
Senator Risa Hontiveros: na dumadanas ngayon ng blackouts,

asr-002163
01:49:15.280 --> 01:49:20.240
Senator Risa Hontiveros: ilang porsyento sa kanila ay may kasiguruhan na

asr-002164
01:49:20.240 --> 01:49:23.040
Senator Risa Hontiveros: kung gusto nila magsindi ng parol ngayong Pasko,

asr-002165
01:49:23.460 --> 01:49:24.740
Senator Risa Hontiveros: magagawa nila ito.

asr-002166
01:49:25.000 --> 01:49:27.940
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Tulad ng unang tinarget ng department noong September.

asr-002167
01:49:28.800 --> 01:49:30.160
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Salamat, Mr. President.

asr-002168
01:49:30.400 --> 01:49:32.100
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Salamat, good sponsor at sa Dio.

asr-002169
01:49:32.220 --> 01:49:32.720
Senate President Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Thank you, po.

asr-002170
01:49:32.920 --> 01:49:33.300
Senate President Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Thank you.

asr-002171
01:49:33.300 --> 01:49:36.620
Senate President Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Thank you, Senator Riza Hontiveros.

asr-002172
01:49:36.720 --> 01:49:38.660
Senate President Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Next will be Senator Aimee Marcos.

asr-002173
01:49:39.020 --> 01:49:40.180
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Maraming salamat.

asr-002174
01:49:40.320 --> 01:49:42.520
Senator Imee R. Marcos: At hindi naman akong mag-interpolate as such,

asr-002175
01:49:43.020 --> 01:49:48.560
Senator Imee R. Marcos: kundi sasabihin lamang na sa ating chairwoman at sa ating sekretary,

asr-002176
01:49:48.560 --> 01:49:50.080
Senator Imee R. Marcos: pati na rin sa ating president,

asr-002177
01:49:50.720 --> 01:49:53.300
Senator Imee R. Marcos: napaka-late na, mag-alas dos na,

asr-002178
01:49:53.300 --> 01:49:55.400
Senator Imee R. Marcos: talagang naglalampumpusa na tayo.

asr-002179
01:49:55.780 --> 01:49:56.680
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Ang akin na lamang,

asr-002180
01:49:56.760 --> 01:49:59.200
Senator Imee R. Marcos: this isn't the first time we've had an oil price shock.

asr-002181
01:49:59.320 --> 01:50:02.780
Senator Imee R. Marcos: We went through it in 1974 and 1979,

asr-002182
01:50:03.060 --> 01:50:06.360
Senator Imee R. Marcos: and without declaring that I'm the oldest person in the room

asr-002183
01:50:06.360 --> 01:50:08.100
Senator Imee R. Marcos: who remembers all this,

asr-002184
01:50:08.680 --> 01:50:10.240
Senator Imee R. Marcos: marami naman tayong ginawa noon

asr-002185
01:50:10.240 --> 01:50:13.200
Senator Imee R. Marcos: na maari pa siguro natin ulitin ngayon,

asr-002186
01:50:13.580 --> 01:50:14.980
Senator Imee R. Marcos: na hindi pa natin nagagawa.

asr-002187
01:50:15.880 --> 01:50:16.940
Senator Imee R. Marcos: At dahil nga,

asr-002188
01:50:17.400 --> 01:50:19.500
Senator Imee R. Marcos: tayo ang pinakamataas sa Southeast Asia,

asr-002189
01:50:19.500 --> 01:50:22.740
Senator Imee R. Marcos: 15 to 16 pesos sa Metro Manila area,

asr-002190
01:50:22.740 --> 01:50:23.740
Senator Imee R. Marcos: per kilowatt.

asr-002191
01:50:24.220 --> 01:50:25.760
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Ang bigat noon, it's so high,

asr-002192
01:50:25.860 --> 01:50:28.240
Senator Imee R. Marcos: in all of ASEAN, we're the highest.

asr-002193
01:50:28.720 --> 01:50:33.700
Senator Imee R. Marcos: So clearly, our neighbors are doing things that we had done before,

asr-002194
01:50:33.920 --> 01:50:35.100
Senator Imee R. Marcos: and that might work.

asr-002195
01:50:35.260 --> 01:50:41.300
Senator Imee R. Marcos: So maraming nagtatanong kung open ang DOE sa iba't-ibang suggestion.

asr-002196
01:50:42.120 --> 01:50:46.920
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Dahil hindi po namin nakikita sa budget ang ganito.

asr-002197
01:50:47.280 --> 01:50:51.640
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Unang-una, yung fixing the outdated power supply agreements,

asr-002198
01:50:51.640 --> 01:50:52.720
Senator Imee R. Marcos: yung mga PSA,

asr-002199
01:50:52.740 --> 01:50:55.780
Senator Imee R. Marcos: yung mga legacy agreements,

asr-002200
01:50:55.900 --> 01:50:57.340
Senator Imee R. Marcos: nasaksakan ng mahal.

asr-002201
01:50:57.760 --> 01:50:59.780
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Nasa 70% ng Meralco,

asr-002202
01:51:00.160 --> 01:51:04.300
Senator Imee R. Marcos: they're still tied to very old, expensive contracts sa Ilocos Norte.

asr-002203
01:51:04.420 --> 01:51:08.160
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Nakatali rin kami dyan sa mga legacy-legacy contracts na yan.

asr-002204
01:51:09.940 --> 01:51:16.080
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Wala bang posibilidad na isuspenso o magdeklarasyon ang DOE?

asr-002205
01:51:16.540 --> 01:51:20.300
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Nateka muna, pwede naman siguro huminahon muna dito

asr-002206
01:51:20.300 --> 01:51:22.720
Senator Imee R. Marcos: sa mga legacy contracts at renegotiation.

asr-002207
01:51:23.280 --> 01:51:26.640
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Anong opinion ni Secretary at ni Chair dyan?

asr-002208
01:51:27.480 --> 01:51:32.540
Senator Imee R. Marcos: They're still tied to all these old, expensive contracts reliant on fossil fuels

asr-002209
01:51:32.540 --> 01:51:38.980
Senator Imee R. Marcos: na para sa amin, sana naging renewable na dahil marami namang kaming renewable sa Ilocos.

asr-002210
01:51:39.720 --> 01:51:42.320
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Pero we're stuck with those contracts, 10 years.

asr-002211
01:51:43.160 --> 01:51:45.820
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Meralco, 70% legacy contract.

asr-002212
01:51:46.260 --> 01:51:47.220
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Pwede bang tignan yun?

asr-002213
01:51:47.400 --> 01:51:48.400
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Suggestion lang po.

asr-002214
01:51:48.800 --> 01:51:51.740
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Tumatangong si Secretary, baka pwede naman isuspend,

asr-002215
01:51:51.740 --> 01:51:52.740
Senator Imee R. Marcos: i-postpone.

asr-002216
01:51:53.600 --> 01:51:56.480
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Yes, they are willing to look into it, Your Honor.

asr-002217
01:51:56.940 --> 01:51:59.380
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Yes, and then another thing is,

asr-002218
01:51:59.720 --> 01:52:03.500
Senator Imee R. Marcos: pag nagkaroon ng gulo na sa WESEM,

asr-002219
01:52:03.620 --> 01:52:07.380
Senator Imee R. Marcos: is it possible that we enforce competitive bidding?

asr-002220
01:52:07.980 --> 01:52:13.520
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Yung competitive selection process for the brand new contracts that we will embark upon?

asr-002221
01:52:13.880 --> 01:52:17.500
Senator Imee R. Marcos: And then remove the automatic fuel pass-through clauses

asr-002222
01:52:17.500 --> 01:52:21.720
Senator Imee R. Marcos: that insulate the power generators from global price hikes?

asr-002223
01:52:21.740 --> 01:52:23.620
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Na tayo lahat ang nag-aabsorb.

asr-002224
01:52:23.980 --> 01:52:28.120
Senator Imee R. Marcos: It could significantly lower baseline rates.

asr-002225
01:52:28.680 --> 01:52:28.920
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Diba?

asr-002226
01:52:29.280 --> 01:52:31.500
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Kasi magiging competitive bidding na yan eh.

asr-002227
01:52:31.560 --> 01:52:32.560
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Pagalingan na yan.

asr-002228
01:52:32.940 --> 01:52:35.680
Senator Imee R. Marcos: And then yung automatic fuel pass-through.

asr-002229
01:52:36.180 --> 01:52:37.240
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Tanggal na lahat dyan.

asr-002230
01:52:37.760 --> 01:52:40.000
Senator Imee R. Marcos: So that's one consideration also.

asr-002231
01:52:42.160 --> 01:52:43.200
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Anong tingin ninyo?

asr-002232
01:52:43.280 --> 01:52:44.820
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Is that something we can consider?

asr-002233
01:52:45.000 --> 01:52:50.800
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: They're already implementing and looking into this competitive selection, Your Honor.

asr-002234
01:52:50.800 --> 01:52:51.560
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Oh, that's great.

asr-002235
01:52:51.560 --> 01:52:54.740
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Kasi I don't see it in the line items of the budgets.

asr-002236
01:52:55.040 --> 01:52:57.960
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Pero siguro nandyan sa operation costs naman ninyo, no?

asr-002237
01:52:58.280 --> 01:52:58.980
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Nagagawin nyo.

asr-002238
01:52:59.060 --> 01:53:00.780
Senator Imee R. Marcos: As long as there's a commitment to that.

asr-002239
01:53:01.300 --> 01:53:02.700
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Kasama na sa policy, Your Honor.

asr-002240
01:53:03.040 --> 01:53:03.740
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Oh, that's great.

asr-002241
01:53:03.900 --> 01:53:05.540
Senator Imee R. Marcos: So that's very good news.

asr-002242
01:53:05.940 --> 01:53:08.780
Senator Imee R. Marcos: And sana tignan ninyo nga yung mga legacy contracts

asr-002243
01:53:08.780 --> 01:53:11.740
Senator Imee R. Marcos: that are burdening so many electric cooperatives,

asr-002244
01:53:11.840 --> 01:53:13.160
Senator Imee R. Marcos: including Meralko itself.

asr-002245
01:53:13.700 --> 01:53:17.340
Senator Imee R. Marcos: And the other aspect that we could embark upon,

asr-002246
01:53:17.400 --> 01:53:21.340
Senator Imee R. Marcos: I don't know, this is a suggestion from an old energy hand,

asr-002247
01:53:21.560 --> 01:53:25.560
Senator Imee R. Marcos: is to clear the transmission and grid bottlenecks.

asr-002248
01:53:26.020 --> 01:53:30.020
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Under the EPIRA, transmission capacity has simply failed to keep pace

asr-002249
01:53:30.020 --> 01:53:31.400
Senator Imee R. Marcos: with power generation.

asr-002250
01:53:31.640 --> 01:53:36.000
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Alam natin yan, yung ibang transmission na dekada 70 pa yan,

asr-002251
01:53:36.100 --> 01:53:37.080
Senator Imee R. Marcos: bulok na bulok na, no?

asr-002252
01:53:37.080 --> 01:53:41.280
Senator Imee R. Marcos: So we have to accelerate the grid upgrades

asr-002253
01:53:41.280 --> 01:53:45.080
Senator Imee R. Marcos: and improve power plant efficiency.

asr-002254
01:53:45.640 --> 01:53:48.280
Senator Imee R. Marcos: May existing power plants that are only operating

asr-002255
01:53:48.280 --> 01:53:51.340
Senator Imee R. Marcos: and the secretary, I've heard you talk about this,

asr-002256
01:53:51.560 --> 01:53:54.980
Senator Imee R. Marcos: they're only at 50% efficiency and capacity.

asr-002257
01:53:55.640 --> 01:53:57.940
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Maswerte ka na kung 80%.

asr-002258
01:53:57.940 --> 01:54:00.420
Senator Imee R. Marcos: So hindi ko alam kung luma ba yan

asr-002259
01:54:00.420 --> 01:54:02.700
Senator Imee R. Marcos: or kung ano ba yung problema nila.

asr-002260
01:54:04.140 --> 01:54:06.980
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Pero yun na naman, wala na naman sa budget,

asr-002261
01:54:07.260 --> 01:54:08.400
Senator Imee R. Marcos: kaya kinakabahan ako,

asr-002262
01:54:09.100 --> 01:54:12.000
Senator Imee R. Marcos: kailan ba maa-upgrade yung aging infrastructure

asr-002263
01:54:12.000 --> 01:54:13.420
Senator Imee R. Marcos: aside from transmission

asr-002264
01:54:13.420 --> 01:54:16.760
Senator Imee R. Marcos: so that we can minimize the unplanned outages

asr-002265
01:54:16.760 --> 01:54:20.740
Senator Imee R. Marcos: and stabilize supply, prevent sudden price hikes

asr-002266
01:54:20.740 --> 01:54:21.540
Senator Imee R. Marcos: and sudden outages.

asr-002267
01:54:21.540 --> 01:54:24.740
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Mahal yun.

asr-002268
01:54:24.840 --> 01:54:28.480
Senator Imee R. Marcos: I know it's expensive, yung mga power plant efficiency, di ba?

asr-002269
01:54:32.980 --> 01:54:37.540
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Your Honor, the response is ERC has already been approving

asr-002270
01:54:38.320 --> 01:54:42.660
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: the submitted proposals for CAPEX of NGCP.

asr-002271
01:54:42.800 --> 01:54:43.340
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Ah, that's great.

asr-002272
01:54:43.460 --> 01:54:44.900
Senator Imee R. Marcos: So we have that to look forward to.

asr-002273
01:54:44.900 --> 01:54:47.620
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Yes, and then in addition, doon naman sa dagdag niyong question,

asr-002274
01:54:47.620 --> 01:54:50.620
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: is for government,

asr-002275
01:54:51.540 --> 01:54:53.080
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: to be allowed to...

asr-002276
01:54:53.080 --> 01:54:55.780
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: For talking to NGCP, to allow government...

asr-002277
01:54:55.780 --> 01:54:59.880
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: To allow government to directly fund or...

asr-002278
01:54:59.880 --> 01:55:02.060
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Undertake the transmission.

asr-002279
01:55:02.320 --> 01:55:04.960
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Okay, so for government to undertake the transmission.

asr-002280
01:55:05.320 --> 01:55:08.780
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Yes, inasmuch as they haven't done anything about it,

asr-002281
01:55:09.020 --> 01:55:11.420
Senator Imee R. Marcos: they haven't modernized, they haven't invested,

asr-002282
01:55:11.880 --> 01:55:14.500
Senator Imee R. Marcos: I think government simply needs to take over.

asr-002283
01:55:14.500 --> 01:55:19.500
Senator Imee R. Marcos: I have also heard the Secretary talk about establishing our own refineries.

asr-002284
01:55:20.380 --> 01:55:21.520
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Right now, we're stuck.

asr-002285
01:55:21.540 --> 01:55:24.540
Senator Imee R. Marcos: We're stuck with one privately owned refinery.

asr-002286
01:55:24.860 --> 01:55:25.840
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Alam na natin yun.

asr-002287
01:55:26.420 --> 01:55:28.680
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Dati-dati, may tatlong refinery.

asr-002288
01:55:29.420 --> 01:55:31.880
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Ano ba ang posisyon ng DOE?

asr-002289
01:55:32.020 --> 01:55:36.240
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Kasi wala rin sa budget ninyo, plano or FS sa refinery.

asr-002290
01:55:36.660 --> 01:55:37.420
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Ano sa tingin nyo?

asr-002291
01:55:37.540 --> 01:55:42.500
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Kasi I heard the Secretary, parang naganahan kami, nabuhayan kami nun eh.

asr-002292
01:55:51.540 --> 01:55:59.480
Senator Imee R. Marcos: I mean, obviously, that's a very, very big investment.

asr-002293
01:55:59.480 --> 01:55:59.700
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Ma'am?

asr-002294
01:56:06.260 --> 01:56:11.000
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Your Honor, PNOC currently, and they do have a budget for it,

asr-002295
01:56:11.260 --> 01:56:14.220
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: the first step is the storage facility.

asr-002296
01:56:14.240 --> 01:56:14.720
Senator Imee R. Marcos: That's right.

asr-002297
01:56:16.380 --> 01:56:19.360
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: And then, the second step is more storage.

asr-002298
01:56:19.820 --> 01:56:21.420
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: And then, they are now in...

asr-002299
01:56:21.540 --> 01:56:23.160
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: They're in talks with...

asr-002300
01:56:23.160 --> 01:56:24.040
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Did you say Middle East?

asr-002301
01:56:24.160 --> 01:56:27.640
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Middle East, other Western countries.

asr-002302
01:56:27.980 --> 01:56:28.880
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: And according to Trump.

asr-002303
01:56:30.760 --> 01:56:31.320
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Yes.

asr-002304
01:56:31.740 --> 01:56:33.820
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: They're in talks with...

asr-002305
01:56:33.820 --> 01:56:36.220
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Wala na, [unclear] na.

asr-002306
01:56:36.220 --> 01:56:41.760
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: They're in talks for refineries, Mr. Your Honor.

asr-002307
01:56:42.060 --> 01:56:45.120
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Actually, that's the other thing that I was going to inquire about.

asr-002308
01:56:45.220 --> 01:56:47.740
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Deploying utility-scale battery storage.

asr-002309
01:56:48.260 --> 01:56:51.060
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Expanding the battery energy storage systems.

asr-002310
01:56:51.060 --> 01:56:51.380
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Yung BESS.

asr-002315
01:56:51.540 --> 01:56:57.580
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Across the country, 7,000 islands to stabilize intermittent wind and solar

asr-002316
01:56:57.580 --> 01:57:00.980
Senator Imee R. Marcos: and cut reliance on expensive diesel peaker plants.

asr-002317
01:57:02.220 --> 01:57:04.620
Senator Imee R. Marcos: That was another consideration, no?

asr-002318
01:57:05.760 --> 01:57:08.300
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Yung utility-scale battery storage.

asr-002319
01:57:09.020 --> 01:57:11.240
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Hinahanap ko rin kasi sa budget ninyo yan.

asr-002320
01:57:11.360 --> 01:57:18.540
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Kasi eto yung mga structural bottlenecks, quite apart from basic household conservation, no?

asr-002321
01:57:18.960 --> 01:57:21.140
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Where we can bring down the cost.

asr-002322
01:57:21.540 --> 01:57:30.320
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: So, your honor, they have policies on best for the storage.

asr-002323
01:57:31.320 --> 01:57:34.620
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Pero kailangan natin bilhin yung battery.

asr-002324
01:57:35.220 --> 01:57:37.700
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Sa private pa rin.

asr-002325
01:57:37.800 --> 01:57:38.660
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Sa private pa rin.

asr-002326
01:57:38.740 --> 01:57:39.680
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Tapos yung requirement nila...

asr-002327
01:57:39.680 --> 01:57:40.460
Senator Imee R. Marcos: So, is there interest?

asr-002328
01:57:40.620 --> 01:57:41.720
Senator Imee R. Marcos: May mag-iinvest dyan?

asr-002329
01:57:41.920 --> 01:57:42.680
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Yes, ma'am.

asr-002330
01:57:42.740 --> 01:57:43.420
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Meron naman daw.

asr-002331
01:57:43.520 --> 01:57:50.440
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: The requirement pa nga is that for a project, 20% of it has battery storage.

asr-002332
01:57:50.440 --> 01:57:51.380
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Which?

asr-002333
01:57:51.380 --> 01:57:58.340
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Which brings me to another topic, and that's to remove the red tape on rooftop and distributed solar.

asr-002334
01:57:58.840 --> 01:58:05.920
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Kasi ang dami-daming red tape, ang dami-daming pirma, wala na si Mig Subiri, isa yung nagre-reklamo lagi.

asr-002335
01:58:06.420 --> 01:58:09.540
Senator Imee R. Marcos: How do we streamline permitting and net metering?

asr-002336
01:58:10.360 --> 01:58:17.480
Senator Imee R. Marcos: The long approval times, o ayan, kasali na LGU dyan, hindi naman lahat kasalanan DOE.

asr-002337
01:58:17.480 --> 01:58:20.480
Senator Imee R. Marcos: And the distribution utilities, they simply discourage...

asr-002338
01:58:21.380 --> 01:58:24.700
Senator Imee R. Marcos: home owners and businesses from installing solar.

asr-002339
01:58:25.260 --> 01:58:31.200
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Nakakapagod ikot-ikotin lahat ng opisyal at magpapirma ng sagkatutak na papel.

asr-002340
01:58:32.100 --> 01:58:38.820
Senator Imee R. Marcos: And even with the new legislative push, yung zero export solar bills natin,

asr-002341
01:58:39.340 --> 01:58:43.200
Senator Imee R. Marcos: the proposal to cut down on renewable hardware costs,

asr-002342
01:58:43.200 --> 01:58:47.460
Senator Imee R. Marcos: ang dami-daming proposal, pero kapag ganong kabagal yung red tape,

asr-002343
01:58:48.420 --> 01:58:50.560
Senator Imee R. Marcos: paano ba itulak yung mga LGU?

asr-002344
01:58:50.560 --> 01:58:56.060
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Dapat ba i-penalize yan, or yung mga utilities, kailangan ba may sanction para kumilos?

asr-002345
01:58:59.440 --> 01:59:04.620
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: On that last point, na ang dami-dami, matagal, so ARTA is now involved.

asr-002346
01:59:04.760 --> 01:59:05.140
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Yes.

asr-002347
01:59:05.260 --> 01:59:07.920
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Because that really is the goal, to simplify it.

asr-002348
01:59:08.340 --> 01:59:12.520
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: So, to distinguish, when there is no net metering involved,

asr-002349
01:59:12.640 --> 01:59:18.680
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: then wala nang mga iba-iba pang permits, they just have to inform the DOE.

asr-002350
01:59:18.680 --> 01:59:20.000
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Oh, that's perfect.

asr-002351
01:59:20.560 --> 01:59:22.620
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Ipahihwating natin sa marami.

asr-002352
01:59:22.740 --> 01:59:26.240
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Kasi marami talaga napuput off dahil ang hirap-hirap.

asr-002353
01:59:26.500 --> 01:59:27.980
Senator Imee R. Marcos: So, tinatamad na sila.

asr-002354
01:59:28.060 --> 01:59:34.100
Senator Imee R. Marcos: The other thing, of course, is that we are always being told that there's millions in green financing.

asr-002355
01:59:34.100 --> 01:59:40.100
Senator Imee R. Marcos: But to unlock state-backed financing sa pag-ibig, sa SSS, sa GSIS,

asr-002356
01:59:40.980 --> 01:59:45.100
Senator Imee R. Marcos: for low-interest microloans, for residential solar and battery setups,

asr-002357
01:59:46.640 --> 01:59:49.360
Senator Imee R. Marcos: it needs a real push.

asr-002358
01:59:50.000 --> 01:59:50.100
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Kasi...

asr-002359
01:59:50.560 --> 01:59:52.720
Senator Imee R. Marcos: We should utilize these institutions.

asr-002360
01:59:53.060 --> 01:59:53.780
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Andyan na yan eh.

asr-002361
01:59:54.200 --> 01:59:56.000
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Nag-aawas na sila sa sweldo eh.

asr-002362
01:59:57.940 --> 01:59:59.020
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Ah, so wala pa?

asr-002363
01:59:59.140 --> 01:59:59.640
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Wala pa.

asr-002364
01:59:59.640 --> 02:00:00.000
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Thank you.

asr-002365
02:00:00.000 --> 02:00:05.880
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Tapos magmuha na tayo dyan sa mga pag-ibig, yung mga yan.

asr-002366
02:00:06.100 --> 02:00:07.260
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Kasi may pera na yan eh.

asr-002367
02:00:07.600 --> 02:00:08.720
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Meron silang energy loan.

asr-002368
02:00:09.060 --> 02:00:09.400
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Meron.

asr-002369
02:00:09.480 --> 02:00:11.340
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Pero what we want is they promote it.

asr-002370
02:00:11.340 --> 02:00:11.640
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Okay.

asr-002371
02:00:12.200 --> 02:00:16.880
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: So, there is like a GSIS and is it also?

asr-002372
02:00:16.880 --> 02:00:19.640
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Yeah, GSIS, SSS, pag-ibig.

asr-002373
02:00:19.640 --> 02:00:19.940
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Pag-ibig loan.

asr-002374
02:00:19.940 --> 02:00:27.160
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: But they are meeting along with the executive secretary, these agencies, to really promote it.

asr-002375
02:00:27.460 --> 02:00:29.820
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Para ma-push talaga ang pag-ibig.

asr-002376
02:00:29.820 --> 02:00:31.300
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Hindi nila inoobligay yan eh.

asr-002377
02:00:31.360 --> 02:00:33.660
Senator Imee R. Marcos: They're not offering it as an option.

asr-002378
02:00:33.960 --> 02:00:36.460
Senator Imee R. Marcos: That there should be low interest, micro loans.

asr-002379
02:00:36.720 --> 02:00:40.720
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Pwede kang mag-solar para sa business mo, para sa bahay mo.

asr-002380
02:00:41.020 --> 02:00:42.840
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Hindi nila ino-offer.

asr-002381
02:00:42.840 --> 02:00:50.580
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: And they're working also with the provincial governments to, so that on the local, on the ground.

asr-002382
02:00:50.580 --> 02:00:52.740
Senator Imee R. Marcos: And then makakapagbigay pa ng trabaho yan.

asr-002383
02:00:53.280 --> 02:00:59.800
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Dapat hilain rin yung TESDA at yung mga trade and training institutions.

asr-002384
02:00:59.820 --> 02:01:05.460
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Para silang magturo ng scaling up local installation labor.

asr-002385
02:01:05.680 --> 02:01:10.160
Senator Imee R. Marcos: You will generate lots of jobs just putting up all those solar panels and so on.

asr-002386
02:01:10.820 --> 02:01:13.800
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Dapat mag-training rin yung TESDA para sabay-sabay.

asr-002387
02:01:14.180 --> 02:01:19.600
Senator Imee R. Marcos: And then you will successfully unlock all that government financing.

asr-002388
02:01:22.660 --> 02:01:22.840
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Okay.

asr-002389
02:01:23.160 --> 02:01:26.820
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: So, they're currently doing trainings, as her honor mentioned, and accreditations.

asr-002390
02:01:26.820 --> 02:01:29.820
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: The secretary agrees with that.

asr-002391
02:01:29.820 --> 02:01:36.040
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: She agrees with everything that the, the, our honorable senator from Ilocos said.

asr-002392
02:01:36.160 --> 02:01:37.080
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Thank you very much.

asr-002393
02:01:37.180 --> 02:01:38.620
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Which brings me to Ilocos.

asr-002394
02:01:39.000 --> 02:01:44.140
Senator Imee R. Marcos: And that's to unblock all the stalled renewable energy projects.

asr-002395
02:01:44.640 --> 02:01:46.620
Senator Imee R. Marcos: That's been a real problem.

asr-002396
02:01:46.780 --> 02:01:47.960
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Ang tagal-tagal, no?

asr-002397
02:01:48.040 --> 02:01:53.760
Senator Imee R. Marcos: The transition from imported coal and gas is moving much slower than planned.

asr-002398
02:01:54.100 --> 02:01:57.860
Senator Imee R. Marcos: I looked at the budget for RE and it's business as usual.

asr-002399
02:01:57.860 --> 02:01:59.800
Senator Imee R. Marcos: We know we're in panic mode.

asr-002400
02:01:59.820 --> 02:02:02.100
Senator Imee R. Marcos: It's not business as usual.

asr-002401
02:02:02.280 --> 02:02:05.740
Senator Imee R. Marcos: We have to push and enforce the auction timelines.

asr-002402
02:02:06.300 --> 02:02:10.880
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Ang liwanag ng timeline but less than 20% conform with those timelines.

asr-002403
02:02:11.680 --> 02:02:19.260
Senator Imee R. Marcos: So, the government's first two green energy auctions have been completed but less than 20%.

asr-002404
02:02:19.260 --> 02:02:21.460
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Bakit ganun kababa yun?

asr-002405
02:02:21.960 --> 02:02:23.760
Senator Imee R. Marcos: The majority are facing delays.

asr-002406
02:02:23.900 --> 02:02:28.240
Senator Imee R. Marcos: 80% delay, suspension, right of way, permitting.

asr-002407
02:02:29.820 --> 02:02:31.740
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Ang mga yung tight, o.

asr-002408
02:02:31.740 --> 02:02:32.540
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Uh, one and two.

asr-002409
02:02:34.600 --> 02:02:37.000
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Anong mga may face, one and two?

asr-002421
02:02:53.680 --> 02:02:57.420
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: So, uh, your honor, yung Green Energy Auction 1 and 2

asr-002422
02:02:57.600 --> 02:02:59.560
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: admittedly mabagal talaga.

asr-002423
02:02:59.580 --> 02:02:59.760
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Yes sir.

asr-002424
02:02:59.760 --> 02:03:07.520
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: So they've corrected this and for 3 and 4, they're succeeding.

asr-002425
02:03:08.160 --> 02:03:11.800
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Excited kasi kami dyan. Akala namin talagang yun na yung sagot.

asr-002426
02:03:11.800 --> 02:03:18.740
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Kaso 20% lang ang successful eh. Kaya the hurdles really are structural and need to be overcome.

asr-002427
02:03:19.360 --> 02:03:25.760
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Finally, ito is not entirely a DOE. But at the end of the day, kayo rin ang sasagot ng pambayad.

asr-002428
02:03:25.760 --> 02:03:30.160
Senator Imee R. Marcos: And that is modernizing the cold chain and industrial efficiency.

asr-002429
02:03:30.640 --> 02:03:39.240
Senator Imee R. Marcos: We've been obsessing about headline inflation and of course they encompass by and large food costs as well as the rise in energy prices.

asr-002430
02:03:39.800 --> 02:03:45.340
Senator Imee R. Marcos: So overhauling agricultural logistics is very clearly part of that.

asr-002431
02:03:45.340 --> 02:03:55.740
Senator Imee R. Marcos: And they all rely, all these cold storage facilities of VA, of DAR, they rely very heavily on expensive grid electronics.

asr-002432
02:03:55.760 --> 02:04:01.320
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Electricity and crude oil, diesel, which is now even more expensive than gasoline.

asr-002433
02:04:01.940 --> 02:04:12.840
Senator Imee R. Marcos: So scaling up energy efficient, climate smart cold chain hubs like those piloted under the National Cold Storage Industry Roadmap.

asr-002434
02:04:13.320 --> 02:04:16.620
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Na palagay ko DOE is also part of that planning.

asr-002435
02:04:17.120 --> 02:04:23.240
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Would reduce all that energy waste and stabilize the peak grid demand.

asr-002436
02:04:23.560 --> 02:04:25.580
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Alam naman natin may timing.

asr-002437
02:04:25.760 --> 02:04:29.520
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Ayan eh. At pwede naman siguro i-adjust.

asr-002444
02:04:46.520 --> 02:04:55.640
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Your Honor, there is a fuel transition plan.

asr-002445
02:04:55.760 --> 02:04:58.240
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: To really lower the dependence on fossil fuel.

asr-002446
02:04:58.420 --> 02:04:59.460
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: So that's in place.

asr-002447
02:04:59.460 --> 02:05:04.460
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: And they're working closely with DA to...

asr-002448
02:05:06.320 --> 02:05:10.740
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: For the solarization project.

asr-002449
02:05:11.180 --> 02:05:11.460
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: To...

asr-002450
02:05:12.240 --> 02:05:13.780
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Solarization to...

asr-002451
02:05:13.780 --> 02:05:14.000
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Yes.

asr-002452
02:05:14.400 --> 02:05:15.840
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: To transition.

asr-002453
02:05:16.320 --> 02:05:16.820
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: That's right.

asr-002454
02:05:17.260 --> 02:05:21.960
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Right now the solar irrigation is being distributed by both DA and NIA.

asr-002455
02:05:21.960 --> 02:05:24.960
Senator Imee R. Marcos: And the question now is...

asr-002456
02:05:25.760 --> 02:05:28.980
Senator Imee R. Marcos: What is the best situation with the cold storage?

asr-002457
02:05:29.180 --> 02:05:39.180
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Kasi yung logistics chain very heavily dependent and very, very gasoline and diesel consuming.

asr-002458
02:05:39.960 --> 02:05:49.280
Senator Imee R. Marcos: If there's a way for us to transition that quickly, we will be able to bring both food costs as well as energy costs down in one go.

asr-002473
02:06:27.580 --> 02:06:48.580
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: So, Your Honor, they have discussions with NIA to put together a green energy auction for their water assets.

asr-002474
02:06:48.580 --> 02:06:52.580
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Oh, that's great for the cold storage and other logistics facilities.

asr-002475
02:06:52.580 --> 02:06:54.580
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Magiging green auction rin kayo?

asr-002477
02:06:56.580 --> 02:06:57.580
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: For like the irrigation.

asr-002478
02:06:57.580 --> 02:06:59.580
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Irrigation canals and the dams.

asr-002479
02:06:59.580 --> 02:06:59.920
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Ah, okay.

asr-002479-split-2
02:06:59.920 --> 02:07:04.580
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Yes, that solar irrigation is in place. It's the post-harvest now that's costing so much.

asr-002482
02:07:19.580 --> 02:07:26.580
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: So, sa DA naman, they're talking to them so that yung cold storage nila would be using renewable energy.

asr-002483
02:07:26.580 --> 02:07:32.580
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: So, they're discussing that with them to help them make that transition.

asr-002484
02:07:32.580 --> 02:07:37.580
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Thank you so much for being open to all these suggestions.

asr-002485
02:07:37.580 --> 02:07:41.580
Senator Imee R. Marcos: As I said, this isn't our first rodeo.

asr-002486
02:07:41.580 --> 02:07:43.580
Senator Imee R. Marcos: We've been through this before.

asr-002487
02:07:43.580 --> 02:07:54.580
Senator Imee R. Marcos: And many of these structural roadblocks were present even in the 70s and can be overwhelmed by action on the part of the Department of Energy.

asr-002488
02:07:54.580 --> 02:07:55.580
Senator Imee R. Marcos: And of course, we in the legislature.

asr-002489
02:07:55.580 --> 02:08:02.580
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Of course, we in the legislature will be very happy to support and legislate as necessary.

asr-002490
02:08:02.580 --> 02:08:03.580
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Maraming salamat.

asr-002491
02:08:03.580 --> 02:08:04.580
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Thank you.

asr-002492
02:08:04.580 --> 02:08:06.580
Senator Imee R. Marcos: At inaasahan ko na bababa ang presyo.

asr-002493
02:08:06.580 --> 02:08:10.580
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Yes. Salamat for all your interventions, Your Honor.

asr-002494
02:08:10.580 --> 02:08:16.580
Senate President Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Just to close, I just have a slide to show.

asr-002495
02:08:16.580 --> 02:08:23.580
Senate President Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Susundan ko lang yung mga interpellation ni Sen. Risa dahil windy kami.

asr-002496
02:08:23.580 --> 02:08:24.580
Senate President Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Kaya

asr-002497
02:08:24.580 --> 02:08:28.580
Senate President Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Susundang ko yung kanyang question on pricing.

asr-002498
02:08:28.580 --> 02:08:30.580
Senate President Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: And just one slide.

asr-002499
02:08:30.580 --> 02:08:40.580
Senate President Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: And since we finished ASEAN, tinignan ko yung ASEAN electricity rates, ngayon tayo na mayroong pinakamahal na electricity rates sa ASEAN.

asr-002500
02:08:40.580 --> 02:08:49.580
Senate President Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: At itong slide na ito, ang nagpapahirap sa Pilipinas, ito rin nagpapahirap sa mga Pilipino.

asr-002501
02:08:49.580 --> 02:08:52.580
Senate President Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: At it's no coincidence also na in ASEAN, tayo rin ang...

asr-002502
02:08:52.580 --> 02:08:57.580
Senate President Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: meron pinakamababang economic growth.

asr-002503
02:08:57.580 --> 02:09:00.580
Senate President Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Because mataas ang presyo ng kuryente natin.

asr-002504
02:09:00.580 --> 02:09:05.580
Senate President Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: It's very hard to invite FDIs kung ganito ang presyo ng kuryente natin.

asr-002505
02:09:05.580 --> 02:09:13.580
Senate President Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Kahit na anong roadshow natin sa buong mundo, kahit anong incentives ang ibibigay natin kung mataas ang presyo ng kuryente natin,

asr-002506
02:09:13.580 --> 02:09:16.580
Senate President Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: walang papasok at papasok sa ating bansa.

asr-002507
02:09:16.580 --> 02:09:21.580
Senate President Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: So, this is a challenge to the DOE.

asr-002508
02:09:21.580 --> 02:09:23.580
Senate President Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Especially the ERC.

asr-002509
02:09:23.580 --> 02:09:27.580
Senate President Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Tama ho si Sen. Risa, trabaho to ng ERC.

asr-002510
02:09:27.580 --> 02:09:36.580
Senate President Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: At next year with your new budget, we urge you to focus on how to bring down electricity rates.

asr-002511
02:09:36.580 --> 02:09:38.580
Senate President Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Hindi walang pag-asa ho tayo.

asr-002512
02:09:38.580 --> 02:09:49.580
Senate President Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: In fact, tama po yung sinabi ni Sen. Aimee, maraming over-contracting, maraming legacy PSAs, mabagal tayo mag-reset ang WAC natin,

asr-002513
02:09:49.580 --> 02:09:50.580
Senate President Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: double digit figures.

asr-002514
02:09:50.580 --> 02:09:54.580
Senate President Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Hindi walang pag-asa eh.

asr-002515
02:09:54.580 --> 02:09:59.580
Senate President Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Hindi lang tayo determinadong ibaba ang presyo ng kuryente.

asr-002516
02:09:59.580 --> 02:10:02.580
Senate President Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: So, ito po yung hamon namin sa ERC.

asr-002517
02:10:02.580 --> 02:10:16.580
Senate President Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Dati malaki ang tiwala ko sa ERC pero para ngayon, nawawalan na ako ng tiwala na bababa ang presyo ng kuryente natin dahil meron tayong effective na regulator.

asr-002518
02:10:16.580 --> 02:10:19.580
Senate President Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: So, with that, we have a new budget. We have a new year.

asr-002519
02:10:20.580 --> 02:10:27.580
Senate President Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Ang challenge namin sa ERC and also to the DOE is to lower down our electricity rates.

asr-002520
02:10:27.580 --> 02:10:30.580
Senate President Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: So, maraming salamat, Majority Leader.

asr-002521
02:10:30.580 --> 02:10:31.580
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: May I add, Mr. President?

asr-002522
02:10:31.580 --> 02:10:35.580
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Just to give a quick response to the Senate President.

asr-002523
02:10:35.580 --> 02:10:45.580
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: They have a 10-year energy plan that they would like to show the Senate President where they're changing the energy mix.

asr-002524
02:10:45.580 --> 02:10:47.580
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: So, they'll show you as soon as it's ready.

asr-002525
02:10:47.580 --> 02:10:49.580
Senator Juan Miguel "Migz" F. Zubiri: May I just add also, Mr. President, if I may?

asr-002526
02:10:50.580 --> 02:10:57.580
Senator Juan Miguel "Migz" F. Zubiri: On the questions raised by our colleagues, also one of Senator Ivey on the art, on the ease of doing business,

asr-002527
02:10:57.580 --> 02:11:01.580
Senator Juan Miguel "Migz" F. Zubiri: I must say that the DOE has improved immensely.

asr-002528
02:11:01.580 --> 02:11:03.580
Senator Juan Miguel "Migz" F. Zubiri: I'm talking from experience.

asr-002529
02:11:03.580 --> 02:11:05.580
Senator Juan Miguel "Migz" F. Zubiri: They have an EVO system now.

asr-002530
02:11:05.580 --> 02:11:08.580
Senator Juan Miguel "Migz" F. Zubiri: Everything is online, submitted online.

asr-002531
02:11:08.580 --> 02:11:13.580
Senator Juan Miguel "Migz" F. Zubiri: All the dates are accounted for.

asr-002532
02:11:13.580 --> 02:11:18.580
Senator Juan Miguel "Migz" F. Zubiri: They have a certain number of days where they actually release the results.

asr-002533
02:11:18.580 --> 02:11:20.580
Senator Juan Miguel "Migz" F. Zubiri: It's been very efficient.

asr-002534
02:11:20.580 --> 02:11:23.580
Senator Juan Miguel "Migz" F. Zubiri: I have to salute the members of the DOE.

asr-002535
02:11:23.580 --> 02:11:25.580
Senator Juan Miguel "Migz" F. Zubiri: Secretary, you're doing a good job on that.

asr-002536
02:11:25.580 --> 02:11:32.580
Senator Juan Miguel "Migz" F. Zubiri: On the energy mix, the reason why medyo mahal po tayo ngayon, alam po natin may nag-bug down ng mga plants yung Visayas.

asr-002537
02:11:32.580 --> 02:11:35.580
Senator Juan Miguel "Migz" F. Zubiri: Hindi na yung kasalanan ng DOE yan.

asr-002538
02:11:35.580 --> 02:11:39.580
Senator Juan Miguel "Migz" F. Zubiri: Although, talagang alam ko sinisigawan na ni Secretary yan.

asr-002539
02:11:39.580 --> 02:11:45.580
Senator Juan Miguel "Migz" F. Zubiri: And the ERC has already given like show-cause orders to these guys.

asr-002540
02:11:45.580 --> 02:11:47.580
Senator Juan Miguel "Migz" F. Zubiri: And I think they really worked well.

asr-002541
02:11:48.580 --> 02:11:51.580
Senator Juan Miguel "Migz" F. Zubiri: They have a reasonable time to get their plants up and running.

asr-002542
02:11:51.580 --> 02:11:58.580
Senator Juan Miguel "Migz" F. Zubiri: So I think the prices in the Visayas and Mindanao area will stabilize in the next month or so.

asr-002543
02:11:58.580 --> 02:12:01.580
Senator Juan Miguel "Migz" F. Zubiri: So that would stabilize also the prices and bring them down.

asr-002544
02:12:01.580 --> 02:12:04.580
Senator Juan Miguel "Migz" F. Zubiri: Alam naman ni Secretary ang kailangan gawin.

asr-002545
02:12:04.580 --> 02:12:07.580
Senator Juan Miguel "Migz" F. Zubiri: We just have to put more projects out.

asr-002546
02:12:07.580 --> 02:12:12.580
Senator Juan Miguel "Migz" F. Zubiri: No service contracts na hindi gumagalaw.

asr-002547
02:12:12.580 --> 02:12:17.580
Senator Juan Miguel "Migz" F. Zubiri: Dapat ipalabas at itayo nila itong mga service contracts na ito.

asr-002548
02:12:17.580 --> 02:12:23.580
Senator Juan Miguel "Migz" F. Zubiri: But I'm sure we'll have so many players, so much competition that the prices will go down.

asr-002549
02:12:23.580 --> 02:12:25.580
Senator Juan Miguel "Migz" F. Zubiri: So I think patience is needed.

asr-002550
02:12:25.580 --> 02:12:27.580
Senator Juan Miguel "Migz" F. Zubiri: It's really hard at this point in time.

asr-002551
02:12:27.580 --> 02:12:32.580
Senator Juan Miguel "Migz" F. Zubiri: But lalo na El Niño na iyon, napakahirap.

asr-002552
02:12:32.580 --> 02:12:37.580
Senator Juan Miguel "Migz" F. Zubiri: For agriculture, for yung masaya lang sa El Niño, solar power providers.

asr-002553
02:12:37.580 --> 02:12:40.580
Senator Juan Miguel "Migz" F. Zubiri: Pero yung mga hydro power providers, mga hirap na hirap.

asr-002554
02:12:40.580 --> 02:12:44.580
Senator Juan Miguel "Migz" F. Zubiri: But then again, I have to say, there are some good points.

asr-002555
02:12:44.580 --> 02:12:47.580
Senator Juan Miguel "Migz" F. Zubiri: And we can highlight these good points that they've been doing.

asr-002556
02:12:47.580 --> 02:12:50.580
Senator Juan Miguel "Migz" F. Zubiri: I'd like to congratulate the DOE.

asr-002557
02:12:50.580 --> 02:12:53.580
Senator Juan Miguel "Migz" F. Zubiri: And let's give a chance also to the ERC.

asr-002558
02:12:53.580 --> 02:12:55.580
Senator Juan Miguel "Migz" F. Zubiri: New leadership.

asr-002559
02:12:55.580 --> 02:12:57.580
Senator Juan Miguel "Migz" F. Zubiri: They're problem solvers.

asr-002560
02:12:57.580 --> 02:12:59.580
Senator Juan Miguel "Migz" F. Zubiri: They don't look for problems and stick to the problems.

asr-002561
02:12:59.580 --> 02:13:02.580
Senator Juan Miguel "Migz" F. Zubiri: They're problem solvers and that's what we need right now.

asr-002562
02:13:02.580 --> 02:13:04.580
